{"entities":"[{\"text\": \"Procaterol\", \"id\": \"D017265\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"terbutaline\", \"id\": \"D013726\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"bronchial asthma\", \"id\": \"D001249\", \"label\": \"Disease\"}, {\"text\": \"Procaterol\", \"id\": \"D017265\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"bronchial asthma\", \"id\": \"D001249\", \"label\": \"Disease\"}, {\"text\": \"procaterol\", \"id\": \"D017265\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"procaterol\", \"id\": \"D017265\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"terbutaline\", \"id\": \"D013726\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"terbutaline\", \"id\": \"D013726\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"asthmatic\", \"id\": \"D001249\", \"label\": \"Disease\"}, {\"text\": \"tremorgenic\", \"id\": \"D014202\", \"label\": \"Disease\"}, {\"text\": \"procaterol\", \"id\": \"D017265\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}, {\"text\": \"Procaterol\", \"id\": \"D017265\", \"label\": \"Chemical\"}]","filtered_entities":[{"text":"terbutaline","id":"D013726","label":"Chemical"},{"text":"bronchial asthma","id":"D001249","label":"Disease"},{"text":"terbutaline","id":"D013726","label":"Chemical"},{"text":"terbutaline","id":"D013726","label":"Chemical"},{"text":"asthmatic","id":"D001249","label":"Disease"},{"text":"tremorgenic","id":"D014202","label":"Disease"}],"head":"terbutaline","head_id":"D013726","pairs":[{"head":"terbutaline","tail":"bronchial asthma","head_id":"D013726","tail_id":"D001249"},{"head":"terbutaline","tail":"tremorgenic","head_id":"D013726","tail_id":"D014202"}],"relations":["D013726 | D014202"],"result":"$","tail":"tremorgenic","tail_id":"D014202","text":"Procaterol and terbutaline in bronchial asthma. A double-blind, placebo-controlled, cross-over study. Procaterol, a new beta-2 adrenoceptor stimulant, was studied in a double-blind, placebo-controlled, cross-over trial in patients with bronchial asthma. Oral procaterol 50 micrograms b.d., procaterol 100 micrograms b.d., and terbutaline 5 mg t.i.d., were compared when given randomly in 1-week treatment periods. The best clinical effect was found with terbutaline. Both anti-asthmatic and tremorgenic effects of procaterol were dose-related. Procaterol appeared effective in the doses tested, and a twice daily regimen would appear to be suitable with this drug.","metrics":{"precision":0.0,"recall":0.0,"f1":0.0,"rel_tp":0,"rel_fp":1,"rel_fn":1}}